  "mathematical_review": {
    "support": "The original complete-product eta and original dyadic profile yield N^(1-kap0) < n and R(cj)/2 <= n <= 2*R(cj). No smoothing-kap uniformity premise is silently substituted.",
    "quantifiers": "Fix kap0<1 and 0<zeta<=1/20000 before the eventual physical N threshold. Then quantify kap/B/K/cj/j/n/bs or literal row/F.",
    "numeric_supplier": "Instantiate original_chart_numeric_reserves at X=R(cj),a=1,C=2,y=hbCutoff(cj); y^3=2R(cj). hsmall makes 1-18*zeta positive; 3*zeta/4 is positive.",
    "five_gates": "Derive both windows >=1, 64*low^6<n, n<high^3 and hbCutoff<=high. They are conclusions, not new analytic premises.",
    "two_long": "Reuse original_noMedium_actual_alternative on the identical block coefficient and firstMedium selector, then eliminate the one-long branch with the remaining selector.",
    "literal_selector": "singleton_remaining_predicate_iff exactly matches the existing unfolded remainingTypeIValue body on [row]; sourceTest may be used for F with unchanged Q/rho.",
    "scope_limit": "The two-long conclusions retain blockCoefficient != 0. They do not infer aggregate coefficient activity from assignedWeight != 0 and do not bound any discrepancy.",
    "api_review": "Current actualLicence, originalMediumLow/High, originalChart, hbCutoff, typeIValue, profile_nonzero_support and numeric/role supplier signatures were inspected. No concrete mismatch identified.",
